cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenOptima: open-source parametric design optimisation"
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OpenOptima contributors"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/lewisf94/OpenOptima"
abstract: >-
  An engineering optimisation platform that couples parametric CAD geometry,
  automatic meshing and open-source finite element analysis to design of
  experiments and multi-objective optimisation. Regions are identified by
  geometric signature rather than face index so that boundary conditions survive
  geometry rebuilds, and infeasible designs are distinguished from
  infrastructure failures so that solver errors cannot bias the search.
keywords:
  - design optimisation
  - finite element analysis
  - design of experiments
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - CalculiX
  - gmsh
